# Reference for .env.exapp, the connection file of the local HaRP test topology.
#
# Read this file, never copy it. `cp .env.exapp.example .env.exapp` would hand the
# bootstrap a secret that is published in this repository, and APP_SECRET is bearer
# equivalent: whoever knows it can impersonate every account of the instance. The two
# secret lines below are therefore commented out, and the bootstrap refuses any value
# that is not 64 lower case hex characters (CR-02).
#
# The real .env.exapp is written by scripts/bootstrap_exapp.sh and is git-ignored,
# because it carries two working app passwords, the HaRP shared key and the app secret
# of the registration. This example only names the variables.
#
#   export HP_SHARED_KEY="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
#   docker compose -f compose.exapp.yml up -d --wait
#   bash scripts/bootstrap_exapp.sh
#   set -a && . ./.env.exapp && set +a

NC_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081

# The ExApp behind the reverse proxy. Everything the app serves lives under this base.
NC_MCP_EXAPP_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8081/exapps/mcp_connector

NC_MCP_TEST_USER=alice
NC_MCP_TEST_APP_PASSWORD=xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx

# Second, restricted user for the permission tests of the later plans.
NC_MCP_TEST_USER2=bob
NC_MCP_TEST_APP_PASSWORD2=xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx

# The read-only share of plan 05-03, written by ensure_readonly_share: alice owns the folder
# and both files, bob holds the folder read-only and never the private file. The suffix is
# random per instance and pinned across runs; the marker sits in the name and in the content
# of the shared file. Without these four values the permission parity test skips.
NC_MCP_TEST_SHARED_DIR=/mcp-share-0123456789
NC_MCP_TEST_SHARED_FILE=/mcp-share-0123456789/mcp-shared-file-0123456789.md
NC_MCP_TEST_PRIVATE_FILE=/mcp-private-0123456789.md
NC_MCP_TEST_SHARED_MARKER=mcp-shared-file-0123456789

# The registration identity. APP_SECRET is fixed on purpose: a re-registration hands the
# container a new secret otherwise, and a process that still holds the old one answers
# 401 to everything (02-RESEARCH.md, pitfall 11). The bootstrap generates it with
# `openssl rand -hex 32` and writes it into .env.exapp; the line stays commented out here
# so that no copy of this file can ever carry a working one.
APP_ID=mcp_connector
# APP_SECRET=<64 lower case hex characters, openssl rand -hex 32>
APP_VERSION=0.1.0

# Shared between the HaRP container and the daemon registration in Nextcloud. Export it
# before `docker compose up`, the compose file has no default any more.
# HP_SHARED_KEY=<64 lower case hex characters, openssl rand -hex 32>
